.SH NAME
anpu-completion-powershell - Generate the autocompletion script for powershell


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu completion powershell [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for powershell.

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
anpu completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, add the output of the above command
to your powershell profile.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for powershell

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu-completion(1)\fP


